Tracks: ignore drags that started off the grid

A mouse press outside the grid records drag_sx = drag_sy = -1. A following
drag along the same row then took the dy == 0 branch of update_ui_drag,
started a drag at row -1, and copy_and_apply_drag indexed sflags[-w + x]
(heap-buffer-overflow under ASan). Keep such drags inert.

--- a/tracks.c
+++ b/tracks.c
@@ -2079,6 +2079,11 @@
 static void update_ui_drag(const game_state *state, game_ui *ui, int gx, int gy)
 {
     int w = state->p.w, h = state->p.h;
+
+    if (ui->drag_sx < 0 || ui->drag_sy < 0) {
+        ui->dragging = false;          /* the press was off the grid */
+        return;
+    }
     int dx = abs(ui->drag_sx - gx), dy = abs(ui->drag_sy - gy);

     if (dy == 0) {
